From: fxtec-pro1x-guix
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115-pro1x: add the NFC controller

The Pro1X has an NXP NCI controller on I2C1 at 0x28.  The vendor tree
(LineageOS android_kernel_fxtec_sm6115, bengal-idp.dtsi, nq@28) wires its
interrupt to GPIO 70, its enable to GPIO 69 and its firmware download pin
to GPIO 31.  Probed by hand on the phone: a CORE_RESET_CMD at 0x28 is
answered by an NCI 2.0 CORE_RESET_NTF from manufacturer 0x04 (NXP),
hardware 0x41, firmware 01.16.  Its clock request line (GPIO 86) is not
used by nxp-nci.

Ours (fxtec-pro1x-guix, 2026-11-23).

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
index 58d4db6..ba5e228 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
@@ -351,6 +351,16 @@
 		#gpio-cells = <2>;
 	};
 
+	nfc@28 {
+		/* NXP NCI 2.0 controller (hardware 0x41); pins as the vendor tree's nq@28 */
+		compatible = "nxp,nxp-nci-i2c";
+		reg = <0x28>;
+		interrupt-parent = <&tlmm>;
+		interrupts = <70 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+		enable-gpios = <&tlmm 69 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		firmware-gpios = <&tlmm 31 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+	};
+
 	haptics: haptics@58 {
 		compatible = "awinic,aw86224";
 		reg = <0x58>;
